Subject: [PATCH] Preserve full interface init callbacks and adapt unary sites explicitly

GInterfaceInitFunc has two arguments. Keep its public registration macros at
that arity; a shared one-argument trampoline must not erase genuine callbacks.
Known one-argument initializers use explicit GLib unary adapter macros.
Apply after the existing callback-signature portability patch.

--- a/gio/gapplication.c
+++ b/gio/gapplication.c
@@ -294,8 +294,8 @@
 static void g_application_action_map_iface_init (GActionMapInterface *);
 G_DEFINE_TYPE_WITH_CODE (GApplication, g_application, G_TYPE_OBJECT,
  G_ADD_PRIVATE (GApplication)
- G_IMPLEMENT_INTERFACE (G_TYPE_ACTION_GROUP, g_application_action_group_iface_init)
- G_IMPLEMENT_INTERFACE (G_TYPE_ACTION_MAP, g_application_action_map_iface_init))
+ G_IMPLEMENT_INTERFACE_UNARY (G_TYPE_ACTION_GROUP, g_application_action_group_iface_init)
+ G_IMPLEMENT_INTERFACE_UNARY (G_TYPE_ACTION_MAP, g_application_action_map_iface_init))
 
